# AI Assistance and Learning Reflection

## Project: Personal Portfolio Website

**Student:** Olinda Vashi  
**Module:** ELE-IWS-521 – Internet and Web Services

## 1. Introduction

Artificial intelligence tools were used as a supporting resource during the development of my personal portfolio website. The website was designed and developed based on the assignment requirements, my personal interests, and my engineering background.

I used AI assistance mainly to understand unfamiliar concepts, troubleshoot technical issues, explore possible solutions, and improve parts of my implementation. I remained responsible for making development decisions, editing the code, testing the website, and integrating the features into the project.

## 2. Areas Where AI Assistance Was Used

### 2.1 HTML and Website Structure

AI was used to clarify HTML structure and explain how to organize different sections of the portfolio, including the navigation, About section, Skills section, Projects section, and Contact section.

The HTML structure and content were adapted to suit my portfolio design and the requirements of the assignment.

### 2.2 CSS and Responsive Design

AI assistance was used when working on responsive layouts, CSS spacing, navigation styling, hover effects, transitions, and light and dark themes.

I tested the suggested changes in my project and adjusted the CSS to match the design I wanted to achieve. I also made changes to the appearance, typography, backgrounds, and layout of the website.

### 2.3 JavaScript

AI was used to help me understand and troubleshoot JavaScript features such as:

- Mobile navigation.
- Light and dark theme switching.
- Form validation.
- Using `localStorage` to remember the selected theme.
- Fetching information from the GitHub API.
- Filtering and displaying selected repositories.

The JavaScript was reviewed and tested in my project to ensure that the features worked as expected.

### 2.4 Git and GitHub

AI assistance was used to explain Git commands and development workflows, including:

- Creating and switching branches.
- Committing changes.
- Pushing changes to GitHub.
- Creating and merging pull requests.
- Understanding Git status messages and warnings.

I carried out the Git operations in my own project repository and used the workflow to manage the development of different features.

### 2.5 GitHub API Integration

AI was used to help me understand how to retrieve public repository information from GitHub using an API request.

I implemented an API integration that retrieves my public GitHub repositories and filters the results to display selected projects on my portfolio website. I tested the integration and confirmed that the selected project cards were displayed correctly.

## 3. How AI Suggestions Were Verified

I did not rely on AI suggestions without checking them. I verified the changes by:

- Running the website locally in the browser.
- Checking whether the navigation and theme toggle worked.
- Testing the GitHub repository cards.
- Reviewing the code in Visual Studio Code.
- Checking the appearance of the website at different screen sizes.
- Reviewing Git and GitHub results after making commits and merging branches.
- Making additional changes whenever the result did not match my intended design.

## 4. What I Learned

Using AI as a supporting tool helped me improve my understanding of several development concepts, including:

- Organizing a website using semantic HTML.
- Creating responsive layouts with CSS.
- Using JavaScript for interactive website features.
- Working with APIs and asynchronous JavaScript.
- Managing a project using Git and GitHub branches.
- Troubleshooting errors and improving existing code.

I used these explanations to develop my understanding rather than treating AI as a replacement for learning and implementation.

## 5. Limitations of AI Assistance

AI-generated suggestions sometimes required adjustments because they did not always match the existing structure, design, or requirements of my project.

Some suggestions needed to be tested, modified, or rejected before being used. I therefore reviewed the code and made decisions based on how the website was actually working and what I wanted the final portfolio to achieve.

## 6. Reflection

AI assistance was useful during the development of my portfolio, particularly when I encountered technical problems or needed clarification about unfamiliar concepts. However, the project required my own planning, design decisions, implementation, testing, and continuous improvements.

The development process helped me gain practical experience in frontend development, responsive design, JavaScript, API integration, and Git-based project management.

## 7. Declaration

AI tools were used as learning and development support during this project. I remained responsible for the final implementation, testing, modifications, and understanding of the work submitted.